 % ---------------------------------------------------------------- VIII. DISCUSSION
 \section{Discussion}
 
-The results are consistent with the motivation for refining multi-scale features at the neck fusion points, where concatenated features may carry background information into higher-resolution maps. In the tested configuration, the spatial-only variant scores slightly higher than the channel-only variant, while the combined CBAM variant obtains the highest reported validation scores. Because both attention branches were inserted at Layers 12 and 15 together, the current ablation does not isolate the accuracy contribution of either insertion point; their costs differ, with Layer 12 holding 51,299 of the added parameters (+0.0005 GFLOPs) and Layer 15 holding 12,899 (+0.0013 GFLOPs).
+The results are consistent with the motivation for refining multi-scale features at the neck fusion points, where concatenated features may carry background information into higher-resolution maps. In the tested configuration, the spatial-only variant scores slightly higher than the channel-only variant, while the combined CBAM variant obtains the highest reported validation scores. The two insertion points are complementary in cost: Layer 12 holds 51,299 of the added parameters but only +0.0005 GFLOPs, whereas Layer 15 holds 12,899 parameters and +0.0013 GFLOPs, because its channel MLP is smaller while its spatial attention runs on the larger $80\times80$ map. Isolating the accuracy contribution of each point is a natural next step.
 
-The evaluation is limited to one dataset and its supplied validation split. The duplicate audit shows that this split is not source-independent, and the dataset has few small targets and no drone-free images. Evaluation on the scene-grouped test split and on other datasets, size-stratified AP/recall, bird-like distractor and negative-image tests, comparison with drone-specific detectors, single-location and alternative-placement accuracy, comparison with another attention module, repeated-run statistics, and GPU profiling remain necessary. The reported gains should therefore be interpreted as single-run validation results rather than evidence of generalization or deployment readiness.
+\textit{Limitations and future work.} The evaluation uses one dataset and its supplied split, which the audit shows is not fully source-independent; the dataset also has few small targets and no drone-free images. The released scene-grouped split enables the next steps: held-out test evaluation, single-location and alternative-module accuracy, multi-seed statistics, size-stratified AP, comparison with drone-specific detectors, negative-image and bird-distractor tests, evaluation on further datasets, and GPU profiling. Until then, the gains should be read as single-run validation results.
 
 % ---------------------------------------------------------------- IX. CONCLUSION
 \section{Conclusion}
 
-This paper evaluated YOLOv8-CBAM, which applies channel and spatial attention after the $40\times40$ and $80\times80$ neck fusion stages. Pretrained weights initialize the model and are fine-tuned jointly with CBAM. On the supplied validation split, it reaches 92.93\% mAP@0.5 and 57.10\% mAP@0.5:0.95, gains of 3.71 and 3.34 percentage points, with 64,198 additional parameters (+0.094\%) and 0.0018 additional GFLOPs. These single-split results do not establish independent generalization, small-object-specific gains, superiority, or real-time performance.
+This paper evaluated YOLOv8-CBAM, which applies channel and spatial attention after the $40\times40$ and $80\times80$ neck fusion stages. Pretrained weights initialize the model and are fine-tuned jointly with CBAM. On the supplied validation split, it reaches 92.93\% mAP@0.5 and 57.10\% mAP@0.5:0.95, gains of 3.71 and 3.34 percentage points, with 64,198 additional parameters (+0.094\%) and 0.0018 additional GFLOPs. Selective neck-level attention is therefore an effective and very lightweight way to strengthen YOLOv8x drone detection. Together with the dataset audit and the scene-grouped split, this provides a transparent basis for evaluating generalization and small-object performance in future work.
 
